<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (In effect, yes. Neighbouring frames are highly correlated, so the 15% held out overlaps heavily with what was trained on. Every number in this report should be read as an in-distribution upper bound, and a session-level re-evaluation is the first item of future work.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [14]
>>
